// Jest Snapshot v1, https://jestjs.io/docs/snapshot-testing

exports[`rhx enroll — a role modded via .agent/repo=.mods given: [case1] a mod whose of names its linked role when: [t0] a clone is enrolled with the modded role then: the actor boot.md matches its snapshot 1`] = `
"<brief.say path="rhachet/intro">
# rhachet

you are enrolled via rhachet. your roles' briefs and skills follow.

- \`rhx list\` — every skill your roles grant. check it before you improvise
- \`rhx <skill> --help\` — how to call one
- \`rhx init · roles · list · run · enroll · actor · clone · keyrack · ask · act · upgrade\` — the commands; \`rhx <command> --help\` for each

entool: a tactic worth repeat becomes a skill — \`.agent/repo=.this/role=any/skills/<name>.sh\` — so the next clone runs it, never rediscovers it.

</brief.say>

<mod of="test/surfer@0.9.0 (installed 1.0.0)">
role test/surfer@0.9.0 (installed 1.0.0) is modded in this repo — 1 shadow, 1 add, 1 not
[-] not briefs/rule.forbid.wipeouts.md
[~] shadow briefs/rule.require.surf-wax.md drops the published briefs/rule.require.surf-wax.md.min
</mod>

<readme path=".agent/repo=test/role=surfer/readme.md">
# surfer

a test role, as published

</readme>

<brief.say path=".agent/repo=test/role=surfer/briefs/howto.paddle-out.md">
published: paddle out past the break

</brief.say>

<brief.say path=".agent/repo=test/role=surfer/briefs/rule.require.reef-etiquette.md" mod="add">
modded: mind the reef, yield to the inside surfer

</brief.say>

<brief.say path=".agent/repo=test/role=surfer/briefs/rule.require.surf-wax.md" mod="shadow">
modded: wax the board, then wax the rails

</brief.say>

<skill.say path=".agent/repo=test/role=surfer/skills/wax.board.sh">
#!/usr/bin/env bash
######################################################################
# .what = wax the board
#
# .note = sources its peer by its own dir, so a mod that shadows the
#         peer alone is what this skill reads
######################################################################

# [implementation hidden - use skill to execute]
</skill.say>

<skill.say path=".agent/repo=test/role=surfer/skills/wax.lib.sh">
#!/usr/bin/env bash
######################################################################
# .what = the word a waxed board says; sourced by wax.board.sh
######################################################################

# [implementation hidden - use skill to execute]
</skill.say>

"
`;

